# ─── Paths ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Absolute path to the brain/content directory where all data is stored.
# Default: ../../brain/content  (relative to backend/, resolves to repo root)
# Set this only if you want to keep data outside the repo.
# VAULT_PATH=/absolute/path/to/brain/content

# Working directory for the terminal opened via the console button in the UI.
# Default: repo root (two levels above backend/)
# WORK_DIR=/absolute/path/to/repo

# ─── Server ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port the backend listens on.
# Default: 3001
# PORT=3001

# ─── AI provider — pick ONE option below ──────────────────────────────────────
#
# The AI provider powers the web-based onboarding and feed generation.
# If no key is set, those features are disabled and you can still use
# the full app including the CLI path (see CLI_COMMAND below).
#
# Precedence: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY → AI_API_KEY  (first one found is used)

# ── Option A: Anthropic Claude (recommended) ──────────────────────────────────
# Get your key at: https://console.anthropic.com → API Keys
# Models: claude-opus-4-5, claude-sonnet-4-5, claude-haiku-4-5
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-4-5

# ── Option B: OpenAI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Get your key at: https://platform.openai.com → API Keys
# Models: gpt-4o, gpt-4o-mini, o1, o3-mini
#
# AI_API_KEY=sk-...
# AI_API_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o

# ── Option C: Any OpenAI-compatible API (OpenRouter, local Ollama, etc.) ──────
# OpenRouter: https://openrouter.ai/keys  (access 100+ models via one key)
# Ollama (local, free): http://localhost:11434/v1  (no key needed, set any string)
# LM Studio (local, free): http://localhost:1234/v1
#
# AI_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# AI_API_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
# AI_MODEL=anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-5

# ─── CLI tool ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The CLI command opened in Terminal when the user clicks the console button.
# This is how the app launches your AI assistant in the terminal for
# conversational data entry, onboarding, and chat.
#
# Options:
#   claude    — Claude Code CLI  (install: npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code)
#   opencode  — opencode CLI     (install: npm install -g opencode-ai)
#   cursor    — opens Cursor IDE
#   Any other terminal command you want to run.
#
CLI_COMMAND=claude

# ─── Google Calendar (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Enables two-way sync with Google Calendar.
# Setup: https://console.cloud.google.com → Create project → Enable Calendar API
#        → OAuth 2.0 credentials → Desktop app
#
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=...apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
# GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3001/api/sync/oauth/callback
# GOOGLE_TIMEZONE=Europe/Moscow
